{
  "description": "Contract fields the kernel-vocabulary admission manifest holds itself instead of the model (owner decision D9): kernel mapping, subclass and disjointness pins, relation domain/range/direction/strength and mechanics. Extracted once from the comparison that proved them equal to the authored ontology before its deletion; definition text is excluded (the model owns it). Changing a value needs a reviewed update of this file. The kernel_mapping file of DerivesFromNeed and the trace-relation classes follows their move to de4sdv_trace_vocabulary.sysml, and that of the trace-obligation class IncrementTraceObligations its move to de4sdv_increment_workflow.sysml. The rows of the removed classes ApprovedTraceMethod, EvidenceSupportCitation, ScopedEvidenceAdequacyAssessment and ScopedVVActivityRecord, and of the removed relations hasStakeholder and includesCommonCapability, were dropped with them; no other value changed. The rows of the five method-admitted product-line derivation classes (DerivationRule, DerivedVariation, ProductModelProjection, ProductModelProjectionName and UnassignedBindingTime) were added after the deletion: they record the reviewed values of their admission, not an authored-ontology comparison. The rows of the classes ConfiguredProduct, IncrementBaselineDecision and LifecycleDisposition and of the relationship configuredBy, method-admitted by the owner decisions of 2026-10-28 on phases 9 and 12, were added in the same way: they record the reviewed values of their admission, not an authored-ontology comparison.",
